---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Bench & support"
description: "The gear Ferrite is developed and tested with, what it has cost, the licence in plain words, and how to help."
---
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>The bench</h1>
    <p class="lead">Ferrite is built by a small group: developers, testers running it on their own radios, and, we
      hope, more contributors to come. This is the gear it is developed and tested with, what that has cost so far,
      and what would help next. It is here so you can see what goes into the work.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="kicker"><span>01</span>What it has cost</p>
    <div class="figures compact">
      <div class="figure"><b>{{ bench.total }}</b><span>in all</span></div>
      {%- for g in bench.groups %}
      <div class="figure"><b>{{ g.total }}</b><span>{{ g.name }}</span></div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="tablewrap" style="max-width:820px; margin-top:28px">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Item</th><th class="n">Qty</th><th class="n">Cost</th></tr>
        {%- for g in bench.groups %}
        <tr class="group"><th colspan="3">{{ g.name }}</th></tr>
        {%- for b in g.items %}
        <tr><td>{{ b.item }}</td><td class="n">{{ b.qty }}</td><td class="n">{{ b.cost }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- endfor %}
        <tr class="sum"><td>Total</td><td></td><td class="n">{{ bench.total }}</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Canadian dollars, including shipping and tax.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="kicker"><span>02</span>Wish list</p>
    <p class="lead">What would speed up Ferrite's development and let it be measured better, roughly in the order it would help.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap" style="max-width:820px">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Item</th><th>Why</th><th class="n">Estimate</th></tr>
        {%- for w in bench.wish %}
        <tr><td>{{ w.item }}</td><td class="sub">{{ w.why }}</td><td class="n">{{ w.estimate }}</td></tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose" id="licence">
    <p class="kicker"><span>03</span>Licence</p>
    <p>We believe making money from amateur radio goes against the community and the spirit of the hobby. So
      Ferrite is free, its source is public, and it is licensed under the
      <a href="{{ site.licence.url }}">{{ site.licence.name }}</a>. In plain words:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Free, for everyone.</b> Put it on your radios, read the code, change it, and share your changes: you,
        your club, your school, your emergency group. The licence names hobby projects and amateur pursuits
        outright.</li>
      <li><b>Not for sale.</b> Selling Ferrite, shipping it on radios for sale, or selling a service built on it
        needs a commercial licence from us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">This is a summary; the licence text is what counts. It is source-available rather than "open
      source" in the strict sense, because it rules out commercial use.</p>
  </section>

  {% if site.SUPPORT_URL %}
  <section class="section prose" id="support">
    <p class="kicker"><span>04</span>Donations</p>
    <p>We do love donations. They go back into the project: growing it, and more kit to hack on and share what we
      learn. If Ferrite is useful to you, please pay it forward if you can. Testing on your own radio and telling
      us what you find helps just as much.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="{{ site.SUPPORT_URL }}">Donate</a>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="section prose" id="manufacturers">
    <p class="kicker"><span>{% if site.SUPPORT_URL %}05{% else %}04{% endif %}</span>Radio manufacturers</p>
    <p>We would be glad to work with radio manufacturers. Hardware documentation, schematics or sample units would
      let Ferrite support more radios and do it properly, and a manufacturer who wants Ferrite on its radios can
      license it from us. Either way, Ferrite stays free for the people who own the radios.</p>
    <p>And we would love to help spec the next generation of hacker-friendly, open radios: the parts, the pins and
      the documentation that make a radio easy to build on, from what we've learned on this one.</p>
    {% if site.CONTACT %}<p>Get in touch: <a href="mailto:{{ site.CONTACT }}">{{ site.CONTACT }}</a></p>{% endif %}
  </section>
</div>
